<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ayrshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ayrshire is a historic county in south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, on the Firth of Clyde, divided into the districts of Carrick, Kyle and Cunninghame. Inhabited in Roman times by the Damnonii, it later formed part of the British kingdom of Strathclyde. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a> was Earl of Carrick, and the poet Robert Burns was born at Alloway. Its towns include Ayr, Kilmarnock and Irvine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ayrshire.jpg" alt="Ayrshire" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brythones, derivative of Visitor from Wikishire · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayrshire.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
